.TH NOSTR-HOME-SYNCD 8 "2026-09-25" "nostr-homed 0.6.0" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
nostr-home-syncd \- user-scoped portable-home sync daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nostr-home-syncd
[\fB\-\-check\fR | \fB\-\-vault-sync\fR | \fB\-\-vault-retention\fR | \fB\-\-gc\fR [\fB\-\-dry-run\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nostr-home-syncd
is the user-scoped background daemon that watches
.I $HOME
via inotify (only when the session's home is porthome-managed, i.e. the
broker delivered a home seed), chunks and encrypts changed files, uploads them to the
configured Blossom servers, and republishes the kind-30078 pointer when
the batch closes. It always runs as the login user under
.B systemd \-\-user
via
.IR nostr-home-sync.service ;
running as root is a bug.
.PP
The daemon takes configuration through environment variables. The
.B \-\-check
switch validates it offline; experimental vault one-shot switches run the same
reconciler or retention path as the background daemon. Configuration is supplied
in the user unit file. Secret material is delivered to the daemon via a
per-session broker seed drop, described in
.B FILES
below.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exercise the lock, interlock, and ignore-list stacks; report status; exit.
No network traffic, no snapshot, no publish. Safe to run alongside a live
daemon (subject to the lock).
.TP
.B \-\-vault-sync
Experimental vault build only: capture, seal, acknowledge this writer's head,
checkpoint-fold and materialise configured vaults once. Requires the home seed.
An incomplete grant, owner update or cache does not count as success.
.TP
.B \-\-vault-retention
As above, then service the same budgeted lazy re-seal task used by the daemon's
retention maintenance timer. Pending old chunks and held epochs are preserved.
.TP
.B \-\-gc [\-\-dry-run]
Experimental vault build only (also handles personal v1 homes). Mark every
retained generation, current vault writer graph, historical/conflict snapshot,
old-epoch chunk and pending upload/reseal reference before deleting only known
unreferenced porthome/vault candidates with BUD-02. Unknown account uploads stay.
Requires an existing idle sync.lock, the identity signer, and the broker's home
seed handoff; the one-shot reads but does not consume that handoff. Missing or
malformed pin evidence, unavailable relays, missing manifests, unknown vaults,
unsupported reference-state edges or changed heads explicitly refuse deletion.
The daemon schedules the same pass weekly while managed. This is maintenance,
not relay polling; every read boundary requires EOSE from every configured relay.
.PP
Dry-run prints JSON with per-server would-delete rows to stdout and performs no
uploads, deletes, cache fills, seed consumption, or persistent writes (including
budget/status/receipts). Execute mode emits the same report and records the
.B gc
namespace in the existing porthome-status.json; read it with
.B nostr-home-status --json
or
.BR "nostr-home-status --field gc.result" .
Private state files blob-gc-report.json and blob-gc-deletions.jsonl retain the
last result and fsynced per-server attempt/result receipts. An attempt without
an outcome is uncertain, not successful deletion. PUT acknowledgements are
invalidated before DELETE so subsequent reuse must upload again. Historical
snapshot pruning and GC of unknown uploads are deliberately not performed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Required (unless
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_TEST_MODE
is set, see below):
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_NSEC_HEX
64-hex secp256k1 signer for the kind-30078 pointer.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_BLOSSOM
Comma-separated list of https:// Blossom server URLs.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_RELAYS
Comma-separated list of wss:// relay URLs.
.PP
Optional:
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_CONFIG
Strict JSON file containing vaults with path (HOME-relative), vault_id (64 hex)
and is_owner (boolean). IDs and disjoint paths must be unique. Requires the
experimental vault build; invalid or missing explicit files refuse startup
before consuming the broker credential. Configured subtrees and
Portable/.conflicts stay out of personal v1 generations.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_RETENTION_BYTES
Nonnegative decimal sealed-payload budget per weekly retention class; default
134217728. Shared by vault chunk prefetch, lazy re-seal and GC. GC charges
received graph/inventory metadata plus candidate sealed sizes and a 1024-byte
per-delete allowance. It reserves the remaining weekly class before I/O and
refunds unused bytes only after a successful pass; a failed/uncertain pass keeps
the reservation. Dry-run simulates the same remaining allowance without writes.
Reservations persist across restart; authentication/control traffic is outside
this accounting. Private
vault FUSE reads are cache-only: syncd must cache the selected and retained
conflict closures before publishing the namespace. Private-service lazy loading
is unsupported; FUSE receives no signer or authenticated-GET handoff.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_D_TAG
Pointer d-tag override. Default:
.IR nostr-homed.home.v1:personal .
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_MIN_REPLICATION
Minimum Blossom replication before publishing. Default 2. The legacy name
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_MIN_REPL
is accepted for backwards compatibility.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_STATE_DIR
Override the state directory. Default:
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/nostr-homed .
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_HOME
Override
.I $HOME
(tests only).
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_RESCAN_INTERVAL_SEC
Periodic full-tree rescan tick. 0 or unset disables. Non-zero closes
inotify
.B IN_Q_OVERFLOW
and add-watch race gaps.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_MAX_WATCHES
Hard cap on the inotify watches the daemon holds (one per directory).
Default: the smaller of 8192 and a quarter of
.IR fs.inotify.max_user_watches ;
larger values are clamped to half of it. That limit is shared by every
process of the user, and a sync daemon that exhausts it silently breaks
file monitoring in the rest of the session. Directories are watched
breadth-first; those beyond the budget, and well-known noisy trees that are
never watched (VCS metadata such as
.IR .git ,
.IR node_modules ,
language and package-manager caches, anything tagged
.IR CACHEDIR.TAG ),
are still synced through the fallback rescan below. Reaching the budget
logs one warning.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_FALLBACK_RESCAN_SEC
How often the unwatched subtrees are rescanned and diffed against the
snapshot (and re-promoted to watches when budget frees up). Default 600;
0 disables.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_SEED_FILE
Override the broker seed drop path. Default:
.IR /run/nostr-auth/session/<uid>/home_seed .
Read-once, unlinked, mlocked. If it is absent at start the daemon stays
unmanaged (no watches, no scans) and waits for it: inotify on the deepest
existing ancestor of the path, plus a backstop poll. When the drop appears
the home becomes managed without a restart.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_SEED_POLL_SEC
Backstop poll interval, in seconds, while waiting for the seed drop.
Default 30; 0 relies on inotify alone.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_TEST_MODE
When set to 1, permits the (otherwise disabled)
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_SEED_HEX
env fallback so tests can seed home_key without a broker drop. MUST be off
in production.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_SEED_HEX
64-hex seed for home_key derivation. Consulted only when TEST_MODE=1.
.TP
.B NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_SNAPSHOT_MAX_BYTES
Ceiling on the size of
.IR snapshot.json ,
in bytes. Default 1073741824 (1 GiB; a 200,000-entry home is about 64 MB).
The file is stream-parsed, so this bounds memory against a runaway file
rather than a normal home. A larger snapshot is refused (exit 7), never
truncated or replaced.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/nostr-auth/session/<uid>/home_seed
Broker seed drop, mode 0400, owned by the target uid. The daemon reads it
once, unlinks it, and holds the derived home_key in mlocked memory for the
process lifetime.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/nostr-homed/sync.lock
flock() sentinel that prevents two daemons for the same home from running
concurrently. A collision is not an error: the second instance exits 0.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/nostr-homed/snapshot.json
Local baseline of the synced tree. If it cannot be parsed it is renamed to
.I snapshot.json.corrupt.<epoch>
(never overwritten), the baseline is rebuilt by an additive rescan, and
pushes stay refused (partial state) until a pull restores the base. Any
other load failure (too large, newer schema, I/O) stops the daemon with
exit 7 and leaves the file untouched.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/nostr-homed/porthome-status.json
Status file; kept up to date by the daemon. Unresolved conflicts appear
under syncd.home_conflicts and syncd.vault_conflicts, resolution outcomes
under syncd.resolutions.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/nostr-homed/requests/
Conflict-resolution inbox (inotify-watched, scanned once the home is
managed). Each request names a conflict and a choice; the daemon applies
it itself and publishes the result (personal home: HOME edit plus the
normal push of a new generation; shared folder: a signed head, journalled
and committed only after a relay accepts it). Malformed, foreign-owned,
symlinked or oversized files are removed and reported as invalid. Written
by
.BR "nostr-home-status conflicts resolve" (1).
.TP
.I $NOSTR_HOMED_SYNCD_STATE_DIR/home-conflicts.json
Personal-home conflict journal: provenance recorded when the reconciler
keeps both versions (which side the saved copy holds, deletion kind), and
each resolution's intent until its generation is published.
.TP
.I ~/.nostr-home-limited
If present, the daemon refuses to start (\(dqlimited mode\(dq). Used by
admins to disable per-user sync without editing unit files.
.SH EXIT CODES
.RS
.TP 4
.B 0
Clean shutdown, or another instance already holds the sync.lock.
.TP 4
.B 2
Configuration failure (missing NSEC, missing Blossom, missing relays).
.TP 4
.B 3
Refused to run \(em
.I ~/.nostr-home-limited
present.
.TP 4
.B 4
Refused to run \(em NOSTR_HOME_STATE=partial in the environment.
.TP 4
.B 5
Failed to acquire sync.lock for reasons other than contention.
.TP 4
.B 7
.I snapshot.json
unusable: over the size ceiling, written by a newer schema, unreadable,
or corrupt and could not be moved aside. The file is left untouched and
porthome-status.json records the class in
.BR last_error .
With
.BR \-\-check ,
also returned for a corrupt snapshot (the dry run does not quarantine).
.TP 4
.B 8
Vault startup, transport, epoch, policy or materialisation failure. The last
committed namespace and encrypted pending journal are retained. Check the
existing porthome status/error fields before retrying; a missing readback does
not prove an uncertain PUT was rejected.
.RE
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Clean shutdown \(em finish the in-flight batch, publish (or roll back)
the pointer, release the lock, exit 0.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Re-read the per-user quota override written by
.BR nostr-home-status (1)
.BR quota .
.SH SECURITY
Runs as the login user with the systemd
.B User=
directive; never gains capabilities; state and secrets are constrained to
.IR $HOME " and " /run/nostr-auth/session/<uid>/ .
Sets
.B RLIMIT_CORE
to 0. Wipes home_key on exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nostr-homed-provision (1),
.BR nostr-home-status (1),
.BR nostr-home-fuse (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
